    .rpt .rpt-cover-tag { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-on-dark-dim); }
    .rpt .rpt-cover-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.3em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-teal); margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .rpt .rpt-cover h1 { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 58px; line-height: 1.03; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--t-on-dark); margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 12ch; }
    .rpt .rpt-cover h1 em { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; color: var(--t-teal); }
    .rpt .rpt-cover-lede { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--t-on-dark-dim); max-width: 42ch; margin: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-contents { margin-top: auto; padding-bottom: 8mm; }
    .rpt .rpt-contents-title { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-teal); margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .rpt .rpt-contents ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-contents li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr auto; align-items: baseline; padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.22); font-family: var(--t-serif); font-size: 16px; color: var(--t-on-dark); }
    .rpt .rpt-contents li span:first-child { font-family: var(--t-sans); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--t-teal); }
    .rpt .rpt-contents li span:last-child { font-family: var(--t-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--t-on-dark-dim); }

    /* ---- Section kicker and story */
    .rpt .rpt-kick { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; padding-bottom: 8px; margin-bottom: 6mm; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-border); flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-num { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--t-teal-dk); }
    .rpt .rpt-h { font-family: var(--t-sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-ink); margin: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: 7mm; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 6mm; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-stat { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 64px; line-height: 0.9; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--t-accent); }
    .rpt .rpt-stat-label { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.35; color: var(--t-ink); margin-top: 8px; }
    .rpt .rpt-story h3 { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--t-ink); margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .rpt .rpt-story p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .rpt .rpt-findings { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 8px 0 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-findings li { position: relative; padding: 6px 0 6px 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--t-border); font-size: 12px; }
    .rpt .rpt-findings li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 13px; width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--t-teal); }
    .rpt .rpt-findings b { color: var(--t-ink); font-weight: 600; }

    /* ---- Figures. Fixed heights in mm: a page cannot scroll. */
    .rpt .rpt-figure { margin: 0 0 4mm; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-frame { background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-radius: var(--t-radius); padding: 10px; display: flex; overflow: hidden; }
    .rpt .rpt-frame > * { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-frame .dac-viz-block { background: transparent; }
    .rpt .is-chart .rpt-frame { height: 100mm; }
    .rpt .is-tall .rpt-frame { height: 128mm; }
    .rpt .is-table .rpt-frame { height: 98mm; }
    .rpt .is-table-lg .rpt-frame { height: 150mm; }
    .rpt .is-half .rpt-frame { height: 82mm; }
    .rpt .rpt-cap { margin-top: 5px; font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: var(--t-dim); font-family: var(--t-serif); }
    .rpt .rpt-cap b { font-style: normal; font-family: var(--t-sans); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-ink); margin-right: 8px; }
    .rpt .rpt-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 6mm; }
    .rpt .rpt-split.is-wide-left { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; }

    /* ---- Pull insight */
    .rpt .rpt-pull { margin: 2mm 0 0; padding-left: 14px; border-left: 4px solid var(--t-teal); font-family: var(--t-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.28; color: var(--t-ink); max-width: 36ch; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-pull cite { display: block; margin-top: 8px; font-family: var(--t-sans); font-style: normal; font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-dim); }

    /* ---- Summary page */
    .rpt .rpt-h2 { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-weight: 600; font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--t-ink); margin: 0 0 4mm; }
    .rpt .rpt-scope { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 5mm; padding: 8px 10px; background: var(--t-surface); border: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-radius: var(--t-radius); flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-scope-label { font-size: 9.5px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-ink); }
    .rpt .rpt-filter { width: 220px; min-height: 70px; padding: 6px 10px; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-radius: var(--t-radius); display: flex; }
    .rpt .rpt-filter > * { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-scope-note { flex-basis: 100%; font-size: 10.5px; font-style: italic; color: var(--t-dim); }
    .rpt .rpt-kpis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 4mm; margin-bottom: 6mm; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-kpi { background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-top: 3px solid var(--t-teal); border-radius: var(--t-radius); padding: 8px 12px; height: 34mm; display: flex; overflow: hidden; }
    .rpt .rpt-kpi > * { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
    .rpt .rpt-kpi-value .h-kpi-metric-kpi,
    .rpt .rpt-kpi-value .h-kpi-metric-kpi * { font-family: var(--t-serif) !important; font-weight: 600 !important; background: transparent !important; border: none !important; }

    /* ---- Implications and definitions */
    .rpt .rpt-cards { display: grid; gap: 4mm; margin-bottom: 8mm; }
    .rpt .rpt-card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; gap: 10px; align-items: start; padding: 12px 14px; background: var(--t-surface); border: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-left: 4px solid var(--t-teal); border-radius: var(--t-radius); }
    .rpt .rpt-card-n { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--t-teal-dk); }
    .rpt .rpt-card h4 { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--t-ink); margin: 0 0 3px; }
    .rpt .rpt-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; }
    .rpt .rpt-def { padding: 8px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--t-border); }
    .rpt .rpt-def:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-border); }
    .rpt .rpt-def h5 { font-family: var(--t-serif); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--t-ink); margin: 0 0 2px; }
    .rpt .rpt-def p { margin: 0; font-size: 11.5px; }
    .rpt .rpt-contact { margin-top: auto; padding: 10px 14px; background: var(--t-dark); color: var(--t-on-dark); border-radius: var(--t-radius); font-size: 12px; }
    .rpt .rpt-contact a { color: var(--t-teal); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }

    /* ---- Print. The padding on .rpt-page supplies the margin, so @page has none. */
    @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
    @media print {
      .rpt { background: none; padding: 0; gap: 0; display: block; }
      .rpt .rpt-page { width: var(--t-page-w); height: var(--t-page-h); margin: 0; border: none; border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none; break-after: page; }
      /* Without this you get a blank trailing page. */
      .rpt .rpt-page:last-child { break-after: auto; }
      .rpt .rpt-kpis, .rpt .rpt-figure, .rpt .rpt-card, .rpt .rpt-def { break-inside: avoid; }
    }

  </style>

  <article class="rpt-page is-cover">
    <div class="rpt-cover">
      <div class="rpt-cover-top"><img src="https://cdn.holistics.io/logos/holistics-logo-white.svg" alt="Holistics" /><span class="rpt-cover-tag">Ecommerce report 2026</span></div>
      <p class="rpt-cover-eyebrow">Aug 2023 to Oct 2026</p>
      <h1>State of <em>ecommerce</em> performance</h1>
      <p class="rpt-cover-lede">What 33,010 orders, 759 merchants and 10,264 customers tell us about growth, leakage and where to focus next.</p>
      <div class="rpt-contents"><p class="rpt-contents-title">Contents</p><ol><li><span>01</span><span>Revenue is compounding</span><span>p. 02</span></li><li><span>02</span><span>Nearly 30% of orders never land</span><span>p. 04</span></li><li><span>03</span><span>Growth is global, not concentrated</span><span>p. 05</span></li><li><span>04</span><span>Three categories carry a quarter of revenue</span><span>p. 07</span></li><li><span>05</span><span>The customer base doubles every year</span><span>p. 09</span></li><li><span>06</span><span>What it means for next year</span><span>p. 11</span></li></ol></div>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">Summary</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<h2 class="rpt-h2">Key findings</h2>
<div class="rpt-scope"><span class="rpt-scope-label">Set the scope</span><div class="rpt-filter"><h-block name="f_order_date" /></div><div class="rpt-filter"><h-block name="f_customer_country" /></div><span class="rpt-scope-note">Filters change the charts. The written commentary reflects all data.</span></div>
<div class="rpt-kpis"><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_ld9y" /></div></div><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_acsc" /></div></div><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_business_aov" /></div></div><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_nrin" /></div></div><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_audi" /></div></div><div class="rpt-kpi"><div class="rpt-kpi-value"><h-block name="v_users_count" /></div></div></div>
<ul class="rpt-findings"><li><b>Revenue tripled in a year.</b> From $345K in Sep 2025 to $1.06M in Sep 2026.</li><li><b>Growth is volume-led.</b> Average order value has held near $350.</li><li><b>Nearly 30% of orders are cancelled or refunded,</b> about $3.4M of reported revenue.</li><li><b>No market dominates.</b> The largest is 12% of revenue, and Singapore is half its peers.</li><li><b>The customer base doubles every year,</b> and women generate 68% of revenue.</li></ul>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">01 Revenue</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">01</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Revenue is compounding</h2></div><div class="rpt-story"><div><div class="rpt-stat">3&times;</div><div class="rpt-stat-label">revenue versus a year earlier</div></div><div><h3>Steady growth since mid-2024, with one sharp dip</h3><p>Monthly revenue grew from $345K in Sep 2025 to $1.06M in Sep 2026, up from about $90K a month in mid-2024. The one sharp dip came in Apr 2025, down 38% from March.</p><ul class="rpt-findings"><li>Average order value stays near $350, so growth comes from <b>more orders, not bigger baskets</b>.</li><li>Revenue passed its March 2025 level again by August.</li><li>Oct 2026 is a partial month, so its short bar is not a decline.</li></ul></div></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-tall"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_fofr" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 1</b>Revenue by order month. The latest month is partial.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">01 Revenue</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">01</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Revenue is compounding, continued</h2></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-table-lg"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_business_kpi_table" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 2</b>Monthly KPI overview: orders, revenue and average order value.</figcaption></figure><blockquote class="rpt-pull">Growth is coming from more orders, not bigger baskets.<cite>Key insight</cite></blockquote>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">02 Order mix</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">02</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Nearly 30% of orders never land</h2></div><div class="rpt-story"><div><div class="rpt-stat">$3.4M</div><div class="rpt-stat-label">of reported revenue is cancelled or refunded</div></div><div><h3>Seven in ten orders are delivered</h3><p>Of 33,010 orders, 23,174 (70%) were delivered, 8,153 (25%) were cancelled and 1,683 (5%) were refunded. Reported revenue includes these orders, so the leak shows in the headline number.</p><ul class="rpt-findings"><li>Cancelled orders account for <b>$2.85M, or 25%</b> of reported revenue.</li><li>Refunds add another $0.59M (5%).</li><li>Every 10% fewer cancellations is worth about $285K.</li></ul></div></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-tall"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_quxa" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 3</b>Revenue by order status. Cancelled and refunded orders are included.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">03 Markets</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">03</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Growth is global, not concentrated</h2></div><div class="rpt-story"><div><div class="rpt-stat">12%</div><div class="rpt-stat-label">share of revenue from the largest market</div></div><div><h3>Ten markets, none dominant</h3><p>The United States is the largest market at $1.34M. Nine of the ten countries each contribute between $1.1M and $1.3M.</p><ul class="rpt-findings"><li>The United States, Vietnam, Australia and Germany lead.</li><li>The top market is only 18% ahead of the ninth.</li><li>Revenue is well diversified across regions.</li></ul></div></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-tall"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_business_map" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 4</b>Revenue map by country.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">03 Markets</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">03</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Growth is global, not concentrated, continued</h2></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-tall"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_sales_country" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 5</b>Revenue by customer country.</figcaption></figure><div class="rpt-story" style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div><h3>Singapore is the gap to close</h3><p>Singapore is the outlier at $0.63M, about half of its peers. Lifting it to the peer average of about $1.2M would add roughly $0.6M.</p></div></div><blockquote class="rpt-pull">Nine of ten markets sit between $1.1M and $1.3M. Singapore, at $0.63M, is the outlier.<cite>Key insight</cite></blockquote>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">04 Products</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">04</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Three categories carry a quarter of revenue</h2></div><div class="rpt-story"><div><div class="rpt-stat">26%</div><div class="rpt-stat-label">of revenue from Body, Living Room and Televisions</div></div><div><h3>Strength spans electronics, fashion and food</h3><p>Body, Living Room and Televisions together earn $3.0M. Body leads at $1.13M, while Bedroom trails at $0.14M. Televisions, T-shirts, Mobiles and Snacks follow closely, each between $0.84M and $0.91M.</p><ul class="rpt-findings"><li>8,731 products from 759 merchants are listed.</li><li>Look for high-price items that still sell in volume.</li></ul></div></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-tall"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_products_categories" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 6</b>Revenue by product category.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">04 Products</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">04</span><h2 class="rpt-h">Three categories carry a quarter of revenue, continued</h2></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-table"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_products_table" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 7</b>Top products.</figcaption></figure><figure class="rpt-figure is-table"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_products_bubble" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 8</b>Price, units sold and revenue by product.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">05 Customers</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">05</span><h2 class="rpt-h">The customer base doubles every year</h2></div><div class="rpt-story"><div><div class="rpt-stat">2.1&times;</div><div class="rpt-stat-label">2026 signups so far versus all of 2025</div></div><div><h3>Acquisition is accelerating</h3><p>Registered users grew from 478 in 2023 to 1,249 in 2024, 2,769 in 2025 and 5,767 so far in 2026. Women generate 68% of revenue ($7.8M versus $3.8M).</p><ul class="rpt-findings"><li>2026 is a partial year and already 2.1 times all of 2025.</li><li>The audience skews female, which is worth reflecting in merchandising.</li></ul></div></div><div class="rpt-split is-wide-left"><figure class="rpt-figure is-half"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_users_signup" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 9</b>User signups by month.</figcaption></figure><figure class="rpt-figure is-half"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_users_gender" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 10</b>Revenue by user gender.</figcaption></figure></div>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">05 Customers</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">05</span><h2 class="rpt-h">The customer base doubles every year, continued</h2></div><figure class="rpt-figure is-table-lg"><div class="rpt-frame"><h-block name="v_users_table" /></div><figcaption class="rpt-cap"><b>Figure 11</b>Top customers by orders and revenue.</figcaption></figure><div class="rpt-story" style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><div><p>Use the table to find accounts for personal outreach or loyalty offers. Filter by country above to see the leaders in one market.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>

  <article class="rpt-page">
    <header class="rpt-head"><span class="rpt-head-title"></span><span class="rpt-head-section">06 Next year</span><span class="rpt-head-period"></span></header>
    <div class="rpt-body">
<div class="rpt-kick"><span class="rpt-num">06</span><h2 class="rpt-h">What it means for next year</h2></div><div class="rpt-cards"><div class="rpt-card"><span class="rpt-card-n">01</span><div><h4>Fix the leak first</h4><p>Almost 30% of orders are cancelled or refunded. Each 10% fewer cancellations is worth about $285K, the fastest win on the table.</p></div></div><div class="rpt-card"><span class="rpt-card-n">02</span><div><h4>Close the Singapore gap</h4><p>Singapore trails its peers by about $0.6M. Understand why before investing in a new market.</p></div></div><div class="rpt-card"><span class="rpt-card-n">03</span><div><h4>Retain the new cohort</h4><p>The customer base doubles every year, so retention matters more each quarter. Order volume is the lever to watch.</p></div></div></div><h2 class="rpt-h2" style="font-size:20px">Definitions and method</h2><div class="rpt-def"><h5>How is revenue calculated?</h5><p>Revenue is the sum of quantity times product price across order items. It includes cancelled and refunded orders.</p></div><div class="rpt-def"><h5>What period does this report cover?</h5><p>August 2023 to October 2026. October 2026 is a partial month.</p></div><div class="rpt-def"><h5>Do the filters change the commentary?</h5><p>No. The written findings reflect all data. The date and country filters change the charts.</p></div><div class="rpt-def"><h5>Which charts do the filters affect?</h5><p>Date: revenue, orders, order status, revenue trend and categories. Country: users, signups, gender and top customers.</p></div><div class="rpt-contact">Questions about the data? Talk to the data team at <a href="mailto:hi@holistics.io">hi@holistics.io</a>.</div>
    </div>
    <footer class="rpt-foot"><span class="rpt-foot-source"></span><span class="rpt-foot-conf"></span><span class="rpt-foot-page"></span></footer>
  </article>
</div>

    ;;
  }
  settings {
    autorun_on_open: true
  }
  explicit_interactions: [
    FilterInteraction {
      from: 'f_order_date'
      to: ['v_ld9y', 'v_acsc', 'v_quxa', 'v_fofr', 'v_products_categories']
      field: r(orders.created_at)
    },
    FilterInteraction {
      from: 'f_customer_country'
      to: ['v_users_count', 'v_users_signup', 'v_users_gender', 'v_users_table']
      field: r(countries.name)
    }
  ]
}
